<http://data.silknow.org/object/88e5dc68-5b89-33af-99f0-cbbc7b50e79e>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Carpet, knotted in silk pile on silk warps, China, Qing dynasty, probably 18th century"@en , "The carpet is composed of bound edges with stitched down silk. Several pieces assembled for boarder; piece has been cut down for larger piece. Colours are a blend of sky blue, pink, yellow and red with round and triangular floral designs."@en ;
